      "title": "Chao Lab Webpage",
      "headings": [],
      "text": "We are graduate students and postdoctoral scholars at the Chao lab in the Section of Ecology, Behavior and Evolution at UCSD . In general, we use bacteriophage and bacterial systems to investigate topics in evolutionary biology. This includes the advantage of sexual reproduction, the molecular clock, and the decay and recovery of fitness due to drift. We are located on the 3rd floor of the Muir Biology Building , in room 3155. PUBLICATIONS LAB MEMBERS Produced by the Biology Computer Services Department, UCSD. Main address: University of California, San Diego, 9500 Gilman Dr., La Jolla, CA 92093-0346 Send questions, comments and suggestions about this website to: rhokanson@ucsd.edu Copyright �2001 Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved. Official web page of the University of California, San Diego",
